# Module layers (`src/modules/<domain>/`)

Use these folders only when needed; skip empty layers. Keep module-level `types/` (do not nest under `domain/` unless types move with a deliberate refactor).

| Layer | Role | May | Must not |
|-------|------|-----|----------|
| `services/` | Client calls to **our** HTTP APIs | `fetch`, FormData, status/error mapping | Business rules, store writes, DOM download |
| `domain/` | Business / product logic | Clip math, validation, retarget policy, pack rules, framing/pick policy; `three` types/math | `fetch`, DOM download, store `.set`, R3F hooks, Tailwind |
| `utils/` | Shareable helpers (little product meaning) | Small pure helpers, session bridges, teardown helpers | Product policies that belong in `domain/` |
| `adapters/` | External boundaries + format/name mapping | Loaders, exporters, zip, download, native tools, vendor mappers | Own React UI; dump all logic here |
| `actions/` | Store-scoped commands (next to the store) | Read/write that store; call domain/utils/adapters/services | Live as a top-level domain folder unless tied to a store |
| `hooks/` / `components/` | React wiring / UI | Compose layers above | Reimplement domain logic inline |

## Naming

- Prefer `actions/` over `handlers/` for store commands
- Bone / clip / file **mappers** live under `adapters/`; registry **policy** lives under `domain/`
- Do not put HTTP client calls in `domain/`, `utils/`, or `adapters/`

## Examples

```typescript
// ✅ services — HTTP to our API
await fetch('/api/v1/fbx-to-glb', { method: 'POST', body: formData });

// ✅ domain — product rule
export function bakeTimeScale(clip: AnimationClip, scale: number): AnimationClip { … }

// ✅ utils — generic / runtime helper
export function toTimelineTime(mixerTime: number, duration: number, loop: boolean): number { … }

// ✅ adapters — loader / vendor mapper / native tool
export async function loadClipsFromFile(file: File): Promise<ClipLoadResult> { … }

// ✅ actions — store command
export function selectClip(id: string): void { $clips.set(…); }
```

## Fuzzy placements

- `mixer-session` → `utils/` (runtime bridge, not pure policy)
- Vendor bone mappers → `adapters/bone-vendors/`; `bone-registry` → `domain/`
- `scene-dispose` → `utils/`; `model-framing` / `object-pick` → `domain/`

## NFR-2

No R3F / Tailwind / GSAP in `services/`, `domain/`, or `utils/`. `three` in `domain/` / `utils/` is OK for 3D code; keep DOM and network in `adapters/` / `services/`.
